    3) Employment :  providing information on type of work and work status such as 
    major occupation and industry.  
    4) Fertility : such as marital status, number of children ever born, number of living 
    children and dead children.  
    5)  Migration : providing information on migration characteristics of the population 
    such as place of birth, duration of living in current place and reasons for migration.  
    6) Housing :  providing information on level of living and wellbeing of population 
    such as type and characteristics of dwelling, tenure of dwelling, use of light and toilet facility, 
