    1.5  Religion and nationality 
    Most of the population in the Bangkok were Buddhist (92.5 percent), followed by 
    Islamic (4.6 percent) and Christian (19.0 percent).  
    The majority of opulation, of about 91.4 percent were Thais, 2.6 percent was Burmese 
    and the rest were other nationalities such as Cambodian, Chinese and Japanese etc.  
